{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790969422,"nonce":"z4agJ0P2doMeeNIUi5wxQkKYxZo=","message":"Done in 892cb708.\n\nFontTextMeasurer, init_text_measurer and init_text_measurer_with_registry\nnow live in blinc_layout behind the `text_measurer` feature (underscore,\nmatching this crate's existing `clipboard_image` and `media`). blinc_app\nenables it and re-exports all three under their original names, so nothing\ndownstream of blinc_app changes.\n\nTwo blockers the issue flagged, both real:\n\n- preload_generic_fonts was private and never called. It is public now and\n  FontTextMeasurer::new() calls it. with_shared_registry deliberately does\n  not, since a renderer sharing its registry fills the cache itself and\n  preloading there risks a startup font scan.\n- TextLayoutOptions derived Default, so default() gave font_weight 0 while\n  new() gives 400. Nothing is registered at weight 0, so default() missed\n  the cache and measured as an estimate. Default now delegates to new().\n  Worth knowing on the ashui side if you were going to reach for default().\n\nload_system_font and load_font_data are both gone. The first held the only\nblinc_app reference; the second wrote the same unread field and looked like\nit would affect measurement when it could not.\n\nVerified: 42.66px for \"iiiiii\" against 181.22px for \"WWWWWW\" at 32px,\nwhere the estimator reports 105.60px for both. Covered by a test in\nblinc_layout plus examples/standalone_text_measure.rs.\n\nLean builds are unaffected: without the feature, blinc_text stays out of\nblinc_layout's dependency tree entirely.","files":null}]}